AB  - Pre-service teacher education (PSTE) remains dominated by lecture-based instruction, which limits engagement and lacks personalization. To address these issues, social robots have been introduced to support collaborative learning. As AI-generated input becomes more embedded in robot-supported learning, concerns about bias and misinformation have made critical thinking an essential skill for PSTs. Meanwhile, PSTs play a vital role in bullying prevention, yet many report low self-efficacy in managing such situations. Therefore, this study proposed an ODIP-based human-robot paired learning model, supported by the LEFR self-efficacy framework, aiming to cultivate reflective and confident future educators. An experimental study was conducted with 84 PSTs at a university in China, comparing three groups. Results indicated that integrating HR-ODIP method significantly enhanced critical thinking and self-efficacy. Moreover, Epistemic Network Analysis revealed that targeted feedback from the robot facilitated deeper reflection and more elaborate responses, thereby fostering critical thinking development.
